  {
    "id": "#/texts/69",
    "type": "text",
    "text": "For my father, books were knowledge. They were important to him. And yet he loved his children. What he did next was 39 __. Instead of punishing my brother, he sat down, took the pen from my brother's hand, and then wrote in the book himself, alongside the scribbles John had made: \"___ 40 __ work, 1959, age 2.\" How many times have I looked into your beautiful face and into your warm eyes looking up at",
